# Line endings, declared here rather than left to each contributor's Git configuration.
#
# Without this file the result depends on `core.autocrlf`, which is set per machine: the same
# checkout gives one contributor LF files and another CRLF ones, and a commit made on the wrong
# setting rewrites every line of a file it barely touched. .editorconfig already asks editors for
# LF (`end_of_line = lf`); this asks Git for the same thing, so what is checked out matches what
# an editor will write, on every platform.

# Every text file: stored LF in the repository and written LF into the working tree. Git decides
# which files are text by inspecting them, so anything binary is left alone even here.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The plugin's icon and gallery images. Already covered by the auto-detection above; named
# explicitly so a hand-edited or unusually-encoded image can never be mistaken for text and have
# its bytes rewritten.
*.png binary
